WEBVTT

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:07.460
<i>Can't you see that you are sweet?</i>

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:15.050
<i>Oh, let me love you so.</i>

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:24.460
War in the Pocket

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:31.150
<i>As I look up, the sky above seems so far away...</i>

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:31.150
<i>miageru sora wa tooi kedo</i>

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:37.320
<i>...but there are dreams that even it can't hold.</i>

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:37.320
<i>kakae kirenai yume ga aru</i>

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:48.290
<i>Oh, yes, I want to slip away from this artificial world...</i>

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:48.290
<i>sou yo, tsukurareta sekai no naka wo mukidashite</i>

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:52.670
<i>...and make myself free.</i>

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:52.670
<i>jiyuu ni naritai</i>

00:00:52.750 --> 00:01:06.890
<i>I can keep on running till I finally reach the sky.</i>

00:00:52.750 --> 00:01:06.890
<i>hashi ni tsuzukete sora ni todoteba</i>

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:17.280
<i>Since I can believe that I can become the wind someday...</i>

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:17.280
<i>kaze ni nareru to sou shinjiteru kara</i>

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:23.450
<i>I never give up forever.</i>

00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:58.170
So, anyway, I set it up over the phone...

00:01:58.210 --> 00:02:00.250
...and then I waited in that restaurant for two hours!

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:03.970
She never even showed up. Two hours, man! Two hours!

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:06.590
I was so persistent, it brought tears to my eyes!

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:09.350
You should use that persistence for better things.

00:02:09.430 --> 00:02:13.310
I finally score some leave, and she ruins it!

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:15.140
Man, of all the lousy luck!

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:19.400
Hey, in life, you win some and you lose some.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:27.700
Bernie!

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:29.950
Al, you little!

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:31.950
I saw a mobile suit!

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:34.500
To hell with the mobile suit!

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:37.170
A GM?

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:39.580
Then what?

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:43.130
I don't know what it's called, but I got pictures of it.

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:46.590
Over the River and Through the Woods

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:50.680
<i>In response to the second</i> <i>treaty violation yesterday...</i>

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:53.680
<i>... by Zeon Forces at Libot colony,</i> <i>the Riah government issued...</i>

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:56.730
<i>... a strong protest to</i> <i>the Principality of Zeon.</i>

00:02:56.770 --> 00:03:00.650
<i>Regrettably, the Principality</i> <i>has refused to apologize.</i>

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:04.230
<i>A cabinet bill barring</i> <i>Zeon ships from...</i>

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:08.780
<i>... all colonies in Riah was</i> <i>submitted to the assembly today.</i>

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:13.080
<i>It was voted on and</i> <i>approved by a wide majority.</i>

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:17.330
<i>A spokesman for the Ministry</i> <i>of Foreign Affairs stated...</i>

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:20.670
<i>... that all Zeon ships will</i> <i>be deported in a day or so.</i>

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:39.980
Sorry, we're closed.

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:42.690
Didn't you hear me? I said we're closed!

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:44.980
You got any flat beer?

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:48.240
That's a hell of an order.

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:51.070
I won't mind, as long as it's better than horse piss.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.570
I may have some in back.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:54.950
I'd appreciate it.

00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:58.580
A Feddie base, huh? That's a big thing to look for.

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:01.960
We think they may be using a rented-out civilian facility.

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:05.380
This may take awhile. Wait for me at the counter, will you?

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:10.720
- Sorry for the wait
- No prob. You found it?

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:15.140
Just the location. Looks like they're using a converted factory.

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:17.640
There's a map and the factory blueprints in there.

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:21.230
The blueprints are from before the renovations, so don't rely on them.

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:23.770
Thanks for the help.

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:26.440
And give that letter to Steiner, would you?

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:27.440
Sure.

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:32.950
You had it in camera mode, right? You sure you got the pictures?

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:34.530
They're fine.

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:37.160
You're a real optimist, you know that?

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:39.290
"Optimist?"

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:41.710
You never think things will go wrong?

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:42.750
Never.

00:04:45.460 --> 00:04:46.840
Check it out.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.100
You idiot!

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:05.150
Are you trying to wreck this mission?! That was a stupid damned stunt!

00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:07.610
What if the Feddies had caught you, huh?!

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:08.940
This isn't a god damned game!

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:10.820
Knock it off, both of you.

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:14.610
Calm down, Garcia. What's done is done.

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:19.410
Garcia, go back to the bar. Order us some costumes.

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:20.700
Aye, sir.

00:05:23.830 --> 00:05:26.170
Bernie, where's the kid?

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:28.000
In the car, sleeping.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:29.800
Drive him home.

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:30.800
Yes, sir.

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:32.840
And never pull a damn fool stunt like this again.

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:35.840
If you don't want to die, you'll follow orders.

00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:43.600
Al, we're here.

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:46.440
Al, come on. You're home.

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:48.360
Al, wake up!

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:53.650
Oh, well...

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:01.160
Looks just like him.

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:11.630
Terrible likeness.

00:06:28.810 --> 00:06:31.150
Chris, there's someone at the door.

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:33.230
Stay in bed, Mom. I'll get it.

00:06:47.830 --> 00:06:50.130
Let's go out so we don't wake him.

00:06:56.590 --> 00:07:00.550
I'll tell Al's mom he was playing over here and fell asleep.

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:03.680
Thanks, you're a lifesaver. I'd better get going.

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:06.270
See you later, Mr. Wiseman.

00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:10.350
Miss Mackenzie!

00:07:11.650 --> 00:07:12.650
Umm...

00:07:17.860 --> 00:07:20.360
Don't call me Mr. Wiseman, okay? It's Bernie.

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:25.290
Call me Chris. Goodnight, Bernie.

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:26.750
Goodnight.

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:31.130
Chris...

00:07:51.850 --> 00:07:56.280
Oh, it's Mr. G.K. Motor Service. Yeah, they've arrived.

00:07:56.320 --> 00:08:00.820
Extra-strong pliers, heavy-duty drill, special steel-use burner...

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:03.370
You can cut open a battleship with this stuff!

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:06.120
How about a colony wall?

00:08:15.170 --> 00:08:18.630
Your fuses are fine. I also adjusted your breakers.

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:20.590
Thanks, pal.

00:08:40.650 --> 00:08:42.360
Whatcha drawing, Al?

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:43.660
A mobile suit.

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:46.530
Hmm... A Federal Forces one?

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:47.660
A Zeon one.

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:50.830
Huh? Why are you drawing an enemy mobile suit?

00:08:51.370 --> 00:08:53.670
What do you mean "enemy"?

00:08:53.710 --> 00:08:55.960
Don't you ever watch the news?

00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:58.000
Who cares about the news?

00:08:58.050 --> 00:08:59.000
What's up?

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:00.090
What're you doing?

00:09:00.130 --> 00:09:03.380
Chay, he says the Zeon are our enemies.

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:06.850
Yeah, that's right. What's so weird about that?

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:09.430
Telcott, what do you think?

00:09:09.810 --> 00:09:13.350
The Zeon are elitist bad guys. My mom says so.

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:15.690
Is everything your mom says true?

00:09:15.730 --> 00:09:17.400
But grown-ups...

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:23.400
The Zeon are cooler! Zakus are really powerful and GMs suck!

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:26.410
But the best one's the Gundam!

00:09:26.450 --> 00:09:28.200
What's a Gundam?

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:31.660
The Federation's most powerful mobile suit! Don't you know about it?

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:36.080
I've heard of it! It's killed more than 100 Zakus already!

00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:38.880
That can't be true!

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:40.800
It is!

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:42.260
You're really behind the times.

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:45.090
Yeah, the Zeon are scum!

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:47.050
And only scum like scum!

00:09:47.090 --> 00:09:48.430
Did your mom say that, too?

00:09:48.470 --> 00:09:49.890
Al, chill out.

00:09:49.930 --> 00:09:52.980
He's been acting weird lately. He doesn't play with us.

00:09:53.770 --> 00:09:58.150
You guys go back to your seats! Class is starting.

00:09:58.190 --> 00:10:00.400
Cut it out.

00:10:01.650 --> 00:10:04.240
Oh, I get it! You two are going out, right?

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:05.820
- Chay!
- What are you talking about?!

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:08.990
Sorry for butting in. I'll just leave you two lovebirds alone.

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:12.240
Mind your own business!

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:13.700
The teacher's back!

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:16.750
Okay, everyone, quiet down.

00:10:24.760 --> 00:10:27.590
- It's been a long time, Charlie.
- How are you doing?

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:29.220
Still alive, somehow.

00:10:29.890 --> 00:10:31.470
So, what'd you want to tell me?

00:10:32.810 --> 00:10:37.350
You guys are decoys, just here to locate the Gundam.

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:38.900
I knew it.

00:10:38.980 --> 00:10:40.860
You figured it out?

00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:43.820
I asked for a replacement soldier and they assigned me a rookie.

00:10:43.860 --> 00:10:46.700
And then they leave us to find an escape ship on our own.

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:48.910
I'd have to be stupid not to see it.

00:10:48.950 --> 00:10:51.240
I suppose the brass have other plans.

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:02.840
Here are the uniforms you ordered.

00:11:02.920 --> 00:11:05.840
I'll have the passports finished in two nights.

00:11:05.880 --> 00:11:10.590
I'd run if I were you. This war's going to be over soon.

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:12.430
We're going to lose.

00:11:12.470 --> 00:11:13.470
Yeah...

00:11:16.270 --> 00:11:19.230
It's a nice colony, isn't it, Charlie?

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:28.450
What you saw was a new-model Gundam. A Feddie secret weapon.

00:11:28.490 --> 00:11:32.370
A Gundam? Like that one that's shot down a hundred Zakus?

00:11:32.450 --> 00:11:33.990
You know a lot, don't you?

00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:37.000
Can you beat it, Bernie?

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:38.830
Piece of cake!

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:40.540
Piece of cake?

00:11:40.580 --> 00:11:44.040
I'd like to say that, but I'd say our chances are 50/50.

00:11:44.920 --> 00:11:47.510
The Gundam's really powerful, huh?

00:11:47.550 --> 00:11:48.380
Sorta.

00:11:51.720 --> 00:11:55.390
Has Chris been asking about me?

00:11:55.430 --> 00:11:57.350
No, nothing.

00:11:57.390 --> 00:11:58.730
Oh.

00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:04.570
Well, she's a Feddie soldier, right?

00:12:04.610 --> 00:12:08.900
I was thinking, if I got a chance, I could get some good info from her.

00:12:09.610 --> 00:12:11.410
I can try to do that!

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:13.410
I guess that'd be okay, too.

00:12:13.780 --> 00:12:19.160
The blue ones are presumed to be Feddie-controlled buildings.

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:21.580
The red one is the factory where they've stashed the Gundam.

00:12:21.620 --> 00:12:23.330
That's the Feddie base.

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:27.760
The green lines are underground passages. Memorize them all!

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:30.800
I've set up weapons for the mobile suit at three locations:

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:33.140
Here, here, and here.

00:12:35.010 --> 00:12:38.970
We'll blow a hole in the colony hull at this point here.

00:12:39.060 --> 00:12:41.730
It should be big enough for a suit to get out through.

00:12:41.770 --> 00:12:43.480
I set a pretty big charge.

00:12:44.310 --> 00:12:47.690
At 18:00 hours Misha's mobile suit will create a diversion.

00:12:47.730 --> 00:12:51.530
He'll cross from here to the factory perimeter through the city.

00:12:51.570 --> 00:12:53.910
So, by diversion, you mean he'll just be a decoy, right?

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:59.450
I'll be high-tailing it down a busy street. They won't dare attack me.

00:13:01.580 --> 00:13:05.170
The three of us will enter the base through the underground passage.

00:13:05.250 --> 00:13:07.880
We don't know if the Gundam is operational yet.

00:13:07.960 --> 00:13:11.420
If we can't steal it, we'll have to destroy it.

00:13:11.470 --> 00:13:14.800
No matter what happens, after we leave the base...

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:17.180
...we will all escape by different routes.

00:13:17.220 --> 00:13:19.770
We leave at 16:00 hours tomorrow. That is all.

00:13:30.320 --> 00:13:32.860
Never worn body armor before?

00:13:32.900 --> 00:13:33.820
No.

00:13:37.830 --> 00:13:38.370
Bernie...

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:43.960
You're the only guy in this unit who ranks below me.

00:13:45.580 --> 00:13:48.500
I don't want to lose someone I can order around.

00:13:49.590 --> 00:13:51.300
Don't get killed, okay?

00:13:57.970 --> 00:14:03.600
Bernie, I asked Chris and she said I could visit the base!

00:14:04.100 --> 00:14:07.730
<i>I might get a chance to</i> <i>get into that place again.</i>

00:14:07.770 --> 00:14:08.940
When are you going?

00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:09.820
<i>Tomorrow.</i>

00:14:09.860 --> 00:14:12.530
Tomorrow?! No! Al, don't go there!

00:14:12.570 --> 00:14:15.240
But why?! It's a great chance, right?

00:14:15.320 --> 00:14:19.370
I said don't do it and I mean it! You hear me?! Stay away from there!

00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:21.120
Bernie! Bernie!

00:14:45.350 --> 00:14:47.350
To we who are about to die.

00:14:55.650 --> 00:14:57.910
We who are about to die, huh?

00:15:28.810 --> 00:15:29.690
Let's go!

00:15:30.650 --> 00:15:33.610
Prof. Dick Lumunba? Yes, they told us you were coming.

00:15:33.610 --> 00:15:35.900
He's in lab #2 on the fourth floor.

00:15:35.940 --> 00:15:37.150
Thanks, ma'am!

00:15:37.190 --> 00:15:38.490
Oh, don't run in the building!

00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:42.490
Oh, kid, this elevator's for authorized personnel only.

00:15:42.780 --> 00:15:44.740
Visitors have to use that elevator over there.

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:49.460
There are rumors this facility is involved with military research.

00:15:49.790 --> 00:15:51.710
We're just worried that...

00:15:51.750 --> 00:15:55.130
Those are irresponsible rumors with no basis in reality.

00:15:55.130 --> 00:15:58.670
Your research involves mechanical arms, doesn't it?

00:15:59.970 --> 00:16:06.430
Isn't mobile suit technology used to design mechanical arms and legs?

00:16:07.810 --> 00:16:11.150
Toasters and cannons share similar technology, too, you know.

00:16:11.190 --> 00:16:12.150
But...

00:16:14.400 --> 00:16:17.820
Sorry, that'll have to be it for today. I have another interview to give.

00:16:20.280 --> 00:16:25.030
You must be Alfred. My name's Dick. Chris told me about you.

00:16:26.030 --> 00:16:27.580
Are you guys new here?

00:16:27.660 --> 00:16:30.580
Yeah, I just got here a week ago.

00:16:30.660 --> 00:16:31.580
How about you?

00:16:31.670 --> 00:16:33.790
I just got here, too.

00:16:33.830 --> 00:16:38.010
You have a funny accent. Where're you from? Australia?

00:16:38.670 --> 00:16:41.510
Yeah. I was born and raised in Sydney.

00:16:41.550 --> 00:16:43.720
Sydney, huh. Nice place?

00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:47.260
Beautiful. This time of year, the city'd be all covered with snow.

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:29.180
But our forces are mainly equipped with...

00:17:29.220 --> 00:17:32.770
...anti-personnel and anti-tank weaponry! A mobile suit is...

00:17:32.810 --> 00:17:36.270
<i>The Federal Forces will only act</i> <i>as back-up for the Riah Forces.</i>

00:17:36.310 --> 00:17:39.110
<i>We don't want to hear any more</i> <i>complaints from you colonists!</i>

00:17:39.150 --> 00:17:40.030
But, sir!

00:17:40.110 --> 00:17:43.570
I think it'd do your men good to have some real battle experience.

00:17:44.610 --> 00:17:48.080
Bring the <i>Gray Phantom</i> inside! If the suit comes near us...

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:50.120
...form a defense line with the GMs and Guncannons!

00:17:56.420 --> 00:17:59.090
The real problem is the control system.

00:17:59.960 --> 00:18:02.760
It's still too big to be useful for humans.

00:18:03.590 --> 00:18:06.090
But mobile suits are useful.

00:18:06.130 --> 00:18:09.850
Those things are a necessary evil.

00:18:09.890 --> 00:18:12.560
They were never made to bring anyone happiness.

00:18:16.230 --> 00:18:19.980
<i>All personnel, this is not a drill!</i> <i>Everyone, report to your stations!</i>

00:18:20.150 --> 00:18:22.610
<i>The mobile suit is believed</i> <i>to be Zeon in origin.</i>

00:18:22.650 --> 00:18:24.860
<i>It's currently moving</i> <i>down West 18th street.</i>

00:18:25.360 --> 00:18:26.950
Inside the colony?!

00:18:27.780 --> 00:18:30.200
Of course it's operational.

00:18:30.530 --> 00:18:32.410
No response and it hasn't altered its course.

00:18:32.910 --> 00:18:34.960
<i>It'll be passing the</i> <i>residential area soon.</i>

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:38.040
<i>As soon as the civilians</i> <i>are clear, let him have it!</i>

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:49.140
<i>Mobile suit moving rapidly,</i> <i>headed for the residential block!</i>

00:18:50.640 --> 00:18:52.720
<i>This time of year, the city'd</i> <i>be all covered with snow.</i>

00:18:52.930 --> 00:18:54.930
Hey, Sydney boy!

00:18:54.980 --> 00:18:57.140
This time of year, it's <i>summer</i> in Australia!

00:19:07.110 --> 00:19:08.860
These are Zeon guns! Look!

00:19:16.710 --> 00:19:17.790
Bernie!

00:19:36.100 --> 00:19:37.100
Fire!

00:19:45.650 --> 00:19:48.320
Th-Th-The school!

00:19:53.450 --> 00:19:55.450
Scarlet team, launch!

00:20:35.740 --> 00:20:37.330
How's the captain?!

00:20:37.370 --> 00:20:41.000
He's bleeding real bad. I think he's unconscious!

00:20:51.840 --> 00:20:55.970
Scarlet team, destroyed! Enemy mobile suit approaching the base!

00:20:56.010 --> 00:20:57.930
What's happening in the Gundam room?!

00:20:57.930 --> 00:21:00.230
A firefight! We can't get near it!

00:21:00.850 --> 00:21:02.600
Get Lt. Mackenzie down there!

00:21:02.640 --> 00:21:05.230
<i>I'm against this!</i> <i>Fighting inside a colony!</i>

00:21:05.270 --> 00:21:07.980
<i>Would you prefer the enemy</i> <i>get the Alex, Lieutenant?!</i>

00:21:12.780 --> 00:21:14.950
Bernie! We can't steal it now!

00:21:15.320 --> 00:21:17.830
Take the captain and get out of here!

00:21:18.540 --> 00:21:21.960
I'm... I'm gonna blow that thing up!

00:21:23.210 --> 00:21:25.330
Now cover me till I get to it!

00:21:30.090 --> 00:21:30.840
Garcia!

00:21:57.370 --> 00:21:58.950
Lieutenant, it's still dangerous!

00:22:44.000 --> 00:22:46.500
- Wounded?
- Isn't it obvious?!

00:22:46.540 --> 00:22:47.790
The med unit's that way!

00:22:54.670 --> 00:22:56.970
Come on! I'll show you how to fight!

00:23:31.580 --> 00:23:32.380
Wh- What?!

00:24:12.210 --> 00:24:16.380
We've got a breach in the colony hull! Internal pressure, dropping fast!

00:24:16.420 --> 00:24:18.130
What about the Alex?!

00:24:18.670 --> 00:24:21.260
Fog's forming! I can't see!

00:25:20.820 --> 00:25:26.600
<i>On that night I told them that lie...</i>

00:25:20.820 --> 00:25:26.600
<i>uso wo tsuita yoru ni wa</i>

00:25:27.190 --> 00:25:33.330
<i>...I couldn't sleep. That's how scared I was.</i>

00:25:27.190 --> 00:25:33.330
<i>nemurezu ni kowakatta</i>

00:25:33.660 --> 00:25:39.740
<i>But no matter how bad of a fight we would have...</i>

00:25:33.660 --> 00:25:39.740
<i>donna kenka wo shite mo</i>

00:25:40.040 --> 00:25:46.610
<i>...by the next day, it would be forgotten.</i>

00:25:40.040 --> 00:25:46.610
<i>tsugi no hi wa wasureteita</i>

00:25:48.910 --> 00:25:54.090
<i>The sky would be so blue...</i>

00:25:48.910 --> 00:25:54.090
<i>sora ga aoi koto</i>

00:25:55.350 --> 00:26:01.430
<i>...and that would make me so glad.</i>

00:25:55.350 --> 00:26:01.430
<i>sore ga ureshikute</i>

00:26:02.060 --> 00:26:07.940
<i>There would be times when I'd doubt others...</i>

00:26:02.060 --> 00:26:07.940
<i>itsuka hito wo utagai</i>

00:26:08.560 --> 00:26:14.880
<i>...and I'd know the loneliness of living.</i>

00:26:08.560 --> 00:26:14.880
<i>ikiru sabishisa shiru koto mo</i>

00:26:14.940 --> 00:26:20.940
<i>But that was something I didn't notice then.</i>

00:26:14.940 --> 00:26:20.940
<i>ki ga tsukazu ni subete wo</i>

00:26:21.340 --> 00:26:26.380
<i>Back when I believed in everything...</i>

00:26:21.340 --> 00:26:26.380
<i>shinjiteta koro</i>

00:26:49.670 --> 00:26:52.170
NEXT EPISODE

00:26:52.170 --> 00:26:56.090
246 people dead! 572 people wounded!

00:26:56.840 --> 00:26:59.720
They're going to destroy this colony with a nuclear missile.

00:27:00.510 --> 00:27:02.760
People die really easily, don't they?

00:27:03.220 --> 00:27:05.180
I think I'd fight.

00:27:05.220 --> 00:27:06.180
You wouldn't run away?

00:27:12.230 --> 00:27:13.360
That's a lie!

00:27:15.020 --> 00:27:16.990
WAR IN THE POCKET

00:27:16.990 --> 00:27:19.650
Episode 5 Say It Ain't So, Bernie!
